This template is for tracking a release of ADIOS2.

Process this file with the pyexpander script specifying the desired `version`
and the previous release `old_version`:

expander.py --eval 'version="2.9.0"; old_version="2.8.3"' docs/NewRelease.md.tmpl | xclip -selection c

Please remove this comment.
-->
$py(VERSION=str(version.partition("-")[0]))\
$py(MAJOR=int(VERSION.split(".")[0]))\
$py(MINOR=int(VERSION.split(".")[1]))\
$py(PATCH=int(VERSION.split(".")[2]))\
$py(RC="".join(version.partition("-")[1:3]))\
$py(OLD_RELEASE=str(old_version))\
Instructions for performing an ADIOS2 release:

- [ ] Make sure that the milestone for $(VERSION) has no pending issues/PRs.
- [ ] Update your remotes
```
git fetch origin
git fetch github #if needed
```
$if(PATCH == 0 and RC == "-rc1")\
- [ ] Create the release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR) branch from master
```
git checkout -b release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR) origin/master
```
$else\
- [ ] Create a branch that updates the version
```
git checkout -b bump-release-version origin/release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)
```
$endif\
- [ ] Add Commit that updates the version in the repo
```
sed -i 's/^setup_version(.*)/setup_version($(VERSION))/' CMakeLists.txt
sed -i 's/^release = .*/release = "$(VERSION)$(RC)"/' docs/user_guide/source/conf.py
sed -i 's/^\* Latest release: .*/* Latest release: [v$(VERSION)$(RC)](https:\/\/github.com\/ornladios\/ADIOS2\/releases\/tag\/v$(VERSION)$(RC))/' ReadMe.md
git commit -am 'Bump version to v$(VERSION)$(RC)'
```
$if(PATCH == 0 and RC == "-rc1")\
- [ ] Create the tag and push the branch and the tag (no PR is needed)
```
git tag -a -m 'v$(VERSION)$(RC)' v$(VERSION)$(RC) HEAD
# Use the following command with care
git push origin release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR) v$(VERSION)$(RC)
```
$else\
- [ ] Push the branch
```
git push
```
- [ ] Create PR targeting release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)
- [ ] Ask for review
- [ ] Merge PR
- [ ] Create Tag commit `git tag -a -m 'v$(VERSION)$(RC)' v$(VERSION)$(RC) the_merge_commit`
- [ ] Push the tag `git push origin v$(VERSION)$(RC)`
$endif\
- [ ] Create Release in GitHub page
  - Use the following script for getting the PR of this release
    - `./scripts/developer/create-changelog.sh v$(VERSION)$(RC) v$(OLD_RELEASE)`
  - Copy its content to the release description
$if(PATCH == 0 and RC == "-rc1")\
- [ ] Create the `backport release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)` label so PRs can be
  backported to the new branch (see
  [backporting docs](https://adios2.readthedocs.io/en/latest/advice/backporting.html)):
```
gh label create "backport release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)" --description "Backport to release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)" --color e99695
```
$else\
- [ ] Remove older patch releases for $(MAJOR).$(MINOR).X in ReadTheDocs.
$endif\
$if(PATCH != 0)\
- [ ] Record the release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR) history in master without bringing
  its changes (patch release):
```
git fetch origin
git checkout master
git reset --hard origin/master
git merge -s ours release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)
# Be very careful here
git push origin master
```
$elif(RC == "")\
- [ ] If this is the FINAL planned release for release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR), merge
  release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR) back into master, since this release line is
  complete:
```
git fetch origin
git checkout master
git reset --hard origin/master
git merge release_$(MAJOR)$(MINOR)
# Resolve any conflicts, then:
# Be very careful here
git push origin master
```
$endif\
- [ ] Submit a PR in Spack that adds this new version of ADIOS$if(RC == "") (mark this new version as preferred)$endif
  - Run `spack checksum -a adios2` to add it, create commit; push it; Create
    PR in Spack repo.
- [ ] Submit a PR in Conda that adds this new version of ADIOS$if(RC == "") (mark this new version as preferred)$endif
  - CondaForge robot should do this for you automatically, expect a new PR at
    https://github.com/conda-forge/adios2-feedstock a couple of hours after the
    release.
- [ ] Submit a MR for ParaView Superbuild to use v$(VERSION)$(RC) release.
- [ ] Update the website to point to the v$(VERSION)$(RC) release
- [ ] Write an announcement in the ADIOS-ECP mail-list
  (https://groups.google.com/a/kitware.com/g/adios-ecp)
